<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Workflow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <Workflow> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find
        matching parent xml file" error.

        NEW FILE, 2026-08-28. Underwriting__c had no workflow metadata before this change.

        🔴 TWO FIELD UPDATES, NO WORKFLOW RULE, NO REJECTION FIELD UPDATE. Both updates below
        are fired ONLY by approvalProcesses/Underwriting__c.Underwriting_Approval as its
        finalApprovalActions. Do not add a <rules> element: an active rule writing Stage__c /
        Status__c on an ordinary edit would fake an approval.

        🔴 THERE IS NO REJECTION FIELD UPDATE HERE, BY DESIGN (user decision D2). Stage__c never
        changes on rejection - the entry criterion is Stage__c = 'In Progress' and nothing moves
        it during the pending window - so a rejection field update keyed on Stage__c would be a
        same-value no-op even if one were added. On rejection the record simply stays at
        Stage__c = 'In Progress' and only the approval history shows the decision.
        Opportunity.Underwriting_Complete__c is NOT cleared on reject any more (accepted,
        documented regression from the now-inert Opportunity.UW_Reopen_For_Revision) - see the
        approval process file's own header for the full rationale.

        THE CHILD-OBJECT HALF of moving the approval onto Underwriting__c. Both field updates
        write only this record's own fields - required, because Underwriting__c.Opportunity__c
        is a Lookup, not a Master-Detail, so an approval process on this object cannot
        field-update the parent Opportunity at all. The parent mirror
        (UW_Approved__c / Underwriting_Status__c / UW_Approved_By__c / UW_Approval_Date__c) is
        written separately by flows/Underwriting_Approval_Sync.flow-meta.xml, entry-scoped on
        Stage__c transitioning to 'Approved', calling UnderwritingApprovalStampService.

        DEPLOY ORDER - LOAD-BEARING. This file must land BEFORE
        approvalProcesses/Underwriting__c.Underwriting_Approval.approvalProcess-meta.xml, which
        references both field updates by name.
    -->
    <fieldUpdates>
        <fullName>UW_Stage_Approved</fullName>
        <description>Final approval action of Underwriting__c.Underwriting_Approval. Sets Stage to Approved on this Underwriting record.</description>
        <field>Stage__c</field>
        <literalValue>Approved</literalValue>
        <name>UW Stage Approved</name>
        <notifyAssignee>false</notifyAssignee>
        <operation>Literal</operation>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <reevaluateOnChange>false</reevaluateOnChange>
    </fieldUpdates>
    <fieldUpdates>
        <fullName>UW_Status_Approved</fullName>
        <description>Final approval action of Underwriting__c.Underwriting_Approval. Sets Status to Approved by Principals on this Underwriting record.</description>
        <field>Status__c</field>
        <literalValue>Approved by Principals</literalValue>
        <name>UW Status Approved</name>
        <notifyAssignee>false</notifyAssignee>
        <operation>Literal</operation>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <reevaluateOnChange>false</reevaluateOnChange>
    </fieldUpdates>
</Workflow>
